    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. You mentioned \"election integrity\" and \"access versus security.\" When you look at the arguments from the opposition, do you think their concerns about election security are actually a valid way of looking at the issue, or is that just a way to wrap voter suppression in a more palatable term? I need to know if I should treat their claims as fundamental legal concerns or just political rhetoric.",
